{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 1167 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "72e9c25d9d3c36cb325bcc8e02543bddf20575b59217549008d949b6cb87d1f6" :edb/db-before-t 1166 :edb/db-after-t 1167 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534479 50 #inst "2026-10-07T07:39:30.579Z" 13194139534479 true] [17592186100647 1100 "Find the values of $c$ that satisfy the mean value theorem for integrals for  $f(x) = x^2-2x+2$ on the interval $[0,3].$" 13194139534479 true] [17592186100647 1100 "Find the values of $c$ that satisfy the mean value theorem for integrals for $f(x) = x^2-2x+2$ on the interval $[0,3]$." 13194139534479 false] [17592186100647 1145 "Applying the mean value theorem for integrals, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} f(c) (b-a) & = \\int_a^b f(x) \\, \\textrm dx \\\\[5pt] f(c) & = \\dfrac {1}{b-a} \\int_a^b f(x) \\, \\textrm dx \\\\[5pt] & = \\dfrac {1}{3-0} \\int_0^3 (x^2-2x+2) \\, \\textrm dx \\\\[5pt] & = \\left. \\dfrac {1}{3} \\cdot \\left[\\dfrac{x^3}{3} -x^2 +2x\\right] \\right|_0^3 \\\\[5pt] & = \\dfrac {1}{3} \\cdot \\left[ \\left(\\dfrac{3^3}{3} -3^2 +2\\cdot3\\right) - \\left(\\dfrac{0^3}{3} -0^2 +2\\cdot0\\right)\\right] \\\\[5pt] & = \\dfrac {1}{3}\\cdot6 \\\\[5pt] & = 2. \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the expression for $f(x)$ to solve for the value of $c$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf(c) &= 2 \\\\\nc^{2} - 2c + 2 &= 2 \\\\\nc(c - 2) &= 0 \\\\\nc &= 0, 2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534479 false] [17592186100647 1145 "Applying the mean value theorem for integrals, we have\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n       f(c) (b-a)  & =  \\int_a^b f(x) \\, \\textrm dx \\[5pt]\n              f(c)    & = \\dfrac {1}{b-a} \\int_a^b f(x) \\, \\textrm dx \\[5pt]\n    & = \\dfrac {1}{3-0} \\int_0^3  (x^2-2x+2) \\, \\textrm dx \\[5pt]\n     & =  \\left . \\dfrac {1}{3} \\cdot  \\left[\\dfrac{x^3}{3} -x^2 +2x\\right] \\right|_0^3 \\[5pt]\n    & =   \\dfrac {1}{3} \\cdot \\left[ \\left(\\dfrac{3^3}{3} -3^2 +2\\cdot3\\right) -  \\left(\\dfrac{0^3}{3} -0^2 +2\\cdot0\\right)\\right] \\[5pt]\n    & =  \\dfrac {1}{3}\\cdot6 \\[5pt]\n    &  = 2.\n}\n$$\n\n    \n\nNow, we use the expression for $f(x)$ to solve for the value of $c\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(c) & =2 \\\\ {c}^{2}-2c+2 & =2 \\\\ c(c-2) & =0 \\\\ c & =0,2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534479 true] [17592186100648 1100 "Find the average value of the function $f(x) = x - 2$ on the interval $[-2, 4]$." 13194139534479 false] [17592186100648 1100 "Find the average value of the function $f(x) = x - 2$ on the interval $[-2, 4].$" 13194139534479 true] [17592186100648 1145 "Applying the average value formula, we find that the average value of the function is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf_{avg} &= \\frac{1}{b - a}∫_{a}^{b}f(x)dx \\\\\n&= (1)/(4 - (-2))∫_{-2}^{4}x - 2dx \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{6}(\\frac{x^{2}}{2} - 2x) \\mid _{-2}^{4} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{6}[(\\frac{4^{2}}{2} - 2(4)) - (((-2)^{2})/(2) - 2(-2))] \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{6}[(8 - 8) - (2 + 4)] \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{6}(0 - 6) \\\\\n&=-1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534479 false] [17592186100648 1145 "Applying the average value formula, we find that the average value of the function is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}\\,{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4-(-2)}{\\int }_{-2}^{4}x-2\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}-2x){|}_{-2}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}[(\\frac{{4}^{2}}{2}-2(4))-(\\frac{(-2)^{2}}{2}-2(-2))] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}[(8-8)-(2+4)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}(0-6) \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534479 true] [17592186100649 1100 "Find $c$ such that the average value of $g(x) = 3 x$ on the interval $[0,c]$ is equal to $3$." 13194139534479 false] [17592186100649 1100 "Find $c$ such that the average value of $g(x) = 3 x$ on the interval $[0,c]$ is equal to $3.$" 13194139534479 true] [17592186100649 1145 "To solve for $c$, we apply the average value formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ng_{avg} &= \\frac{1}{b - a}∫_{a}^{b}g(x)dx \\\\\n3 &= \\frac{1}{c - 0}∫_{0}^{c}3xdx \\\\\n3 &= \\frac{1}{c}(\\frac{3x^{2}}{2}) \\mid _{0}^{c} \\\\\n3 &= \\frac{1}{c}(\\frac{3c^{2}}{2} - 0) \\\\\n3 &= \\frac{3c}{2} \\\\\nc &= 2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534479 false] [17592186100649 1145 "To solve for $c,$ we apply the average value formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}\\,{\\int }_{a}^{b}g(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 3 & =\\frac{1}{c-0}\\,{\\int }_{0}^{c}3x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 3 & =\\frac{1}{c}(\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{2}){|}_{0}^{c} \\\\ 3 & =\\frac{1}{c}(\\frac{3{c}^{2}}{2}-0) \\\\ 3 & =\\frac{3c}{2} \\\\ c & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534479 true] [17592186100650 1100 "The graph of the function $f(x)$, which is defined on $[1,6]$, is shown below. The areas of the regions between the graph and the $x$-axis are $5$ and $2$, respectively (from left to right). Find the average value of $f(x)$ on $[1,6]$.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1203/Source/Images/348b67f3907c98dd642975d127a3ea0a.png)" 13194139534479 false] [17592186100650 1100 "The graph of the function $f(x),$ which is defined on $[1,6],$ is shown below. The areas of the regions between the graph and the $x$-axis are $5$ and $2,$ respectively (from left to right). Find the average value of $f(x)$ on $[1,6].$ \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/assets/6433d1ca57ceb334f304e894e2655ef50d987567fbcf219314302bb381fd9a83.png)" 13194139534479 true] [17592186100650 1145 "The average value of a function on a given interval is\n\n$$\nf_\\textrm{avg} = \\dfrac{1}{b-a}\\int_a^b f(x) \\: \\textrm{d}x\n$$\n\nHere, we see that\n\n$$\n\\int_{1}^{6} f(x)\\: \\textrm{d}x = -5 + 2 = -3\n$$\n\nSo, applying the average value formula, we find that the average value is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf_{avg} &= \\frac{1}{b - a}∫_{a}^{b}f(x)dx \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{6 - 1} \\cdot (-3) \\\\\n&=-\\frac{3}{5}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534479 false] [17592186100650 1145 "The average value of a function on a given interval is\n\n$$\nf_\\textrm{avg} = \\dfrac{1}{b-a}\\int_a^b f(x) \\: \\textrm{d}x.\n$$\n\nHere, we see that\n\n$$\n\\int_{1}^{6} f(x)\\: \\textrm{d}x = -5 + 2 = -3.\n$$\n\nSo, applying the average value formula, we find that the average value is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6-1}\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534479 true] [17592186100934 1020 #edb/ref 17592186291172 13194139534479 true] [17592186100934 1020 #edb/ref 17592186291179 13194139534479 true] [17592186100934 1020 #edb/ref 17592186291186 13194139534479 true] [17592186100934 1020 #edb/ref 17592186291220 13194139534479 true] [17592186100935 1020 #edb/ref 17592186291193 13194139534479 true] [17592186100935 1020 #edb/ref 17592186291206 13194139534479 true] [17592186100935 1020 #edb/ref 17592186291213 13194139534479 true] [17592186100935 1020 #edb/ref 17592186291238 13194139534479 true] [17592186100935 1020 #edb/ref 17592186291244 13194139534479 true] [17592186100936 1020 #edb/ref 17592186291200 13194139534479 true] [17592186100936 1020 #edb/ref 17592186291224 13194139534479 true] [17592186100936 1020 #edb/ref 17592186291227 13194139534479 true] [17592186100936 1020 #edb/ref 17592186291231 13194139534479 true] [17592186100936 1020 #edb/ref 17592186291235 13194139534479 true] [17592186100937 1020 #edb/ref 17592186291203 13194139534479 true] [17592186100937 1020 #edb/ref 17592186291248 13194139534479 true] [17592186100937 1020 #edb/ref 17592186291252 13194139534479 true] [17592186100937 1020 #edb/ref 17592186291255 13194139534479 true] [17592186100937 1020 #edb/ref 17592186291258 13194139534479 true] [17592186101298 1017 #edb/ref 17592186099389 13194139534479 false] [17592186101298 1017 #edb/ref 17592186291241 13194139534479 true] [17592186101298 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534479 true] [17592186101298 1100 "Find the **exact** value of $c$ that satisfies the mean value theorem for integrals for $f(x) = x^{3} - 3x^{2} + 4$ on the interval $[0, 2]$.$c =$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534479 false] [17592186101298 1100 "Find the **exact** value of $c$ that satisfies the mean value theorem for integrals for $f(x)={x}^{3}-3x+2$ on the interval $[-1,1].$\n\n$c=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534479 true] [17592186101298 1145 "Applying the mean value theorem for the integrals, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(b-a)f(c) & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ f(c) & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ f(c) & =\\frac{1}{1-(-1)}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}({x}^{3}-3x+2)\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{4}-\\frac{3}{2}{x}^{2}+2x)|}_{-1}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[(\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot (1)^{4}-\\frac{3}{2}(1)^{2}+2\\cdot 1)-(\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot (-1)^{4}-\\frac{3}{2}(-1)^{2}+2\\cdot (-1))] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[(\\frac{1}{4}-\\frac{3}{2}+2)-(\\frac{1}{4}-\\frac{3}{2}-2)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{3}{4}-(-\\frac{13}{4})) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(4) \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the expression for $f(x)$ to solve for the value of $c:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(c) & =2 \\\\ {c}^{3}-3c+2 & =2 \\\\ {c}^{3}-3c & =0 \\\\ c({c}^{2}-3) & =0 \\\\ c & =0\\,\\text{or}\\,c=\\pm \\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, since $c\\in [-1,1],$ we take only $c=0.$" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291172 1017 #edb/ref 17592186291173 13194139534479 true] [17592186291172 1089 "q-2472" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291172 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534479 true] [17592186291172 1100 "Find the value of $c$ that satisfies the mean value theorem for integrals for  $f(x)=2x$ on the interval $[1,3].$" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291172 1113 #uuid "656e68c4-9d6b-5e45-8e45-746e2f79d258" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291172 1145 "Applying the mean value theorem for the integrals, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(c)(b-a) & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ f(c) & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3-1}{\\int }_{1}^{3}2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot ({x}^{2})|}_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[{3}^{2}-{1}^{2}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(9-1) \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the expression for $f(x)$ to solve for the value of $c:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(c) & =4 \\\\ 2c & =4 \\\\ c & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291173 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291174 13194139534479 true] [17592186291173 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291175 13194139534479 true] [17592186291173 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291176 13194139534479 true] [17592186291173 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291177 13194139534479 true] [17592186291173 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291178 13194139534479 true] [17592186291173 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534479 true] [17592186291173 1041 "selection" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291173 1104 #edb/ref 17592186291176 13194139534479 true] [17592186291173 1110 #uuid "4b450fdd-891c-5dd6-b21c-7be8da031985" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291174 1034 "3" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291174 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534479 true] [17592186291174 1111 #uuid "e1a22ad5-e500-5af7-92fc-a93dbb8ccb84" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291175 1034 "\\frac{1}{2}" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291175 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534479 true] [17592186291175 1111 #uuid "a3f970e7-b651-55f8-8a31-cfb2d758b43f" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291176 1034 "2" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291176 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534479 true] [17592186291176 1111 #uuid "5fc52018-acb2-55e8-af82-88f6602cbcdb" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291177 1034 "\\frac{3}{2}" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291177 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534479 true] [17592186291177 1111 #uuid "61e1da39-26eb-5d35-8fa6-019f9bf51a8d" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291178 1034 "\\frac{1}{3}" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291178 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534479 true] [17592186291178 1111 #uuid "03bad81c-7a45-5793-bd8e-3e14e5db5df8" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291179 1017 #edb/ref 17592186291180 13194139534479 true] [17592186291179 1089 "q-2477" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291179 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534479 true] [17592186291179 1100 "Find the value of $c$ that satisfies the mean value theorem for integrals for $f(x)=3{x}^{2}-2$ on the interval $[1,3].$" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291179 1113 #uuid "fdd6773f-f519-5a73-aeee-bebe69e14a35" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291179 1145 "Applying the mean value theorem for the integrals, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(c)(b-a) & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ f(c) & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3-1}{\\int }_{1}^{3}(3{x}^{2}-2)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot ({x}^{3}-2x)|}_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[({3}^{3}-2\\cdot 3)-({1}^{3}-2\\cdot 1)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(21+1) \\\\  & =11.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the expression for $f(x)$ to solve for the value of $c:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(c) & =11 \\\\ 3{c}^{2}-2 & =11 \\\\ 3{c}^{2} & =13 \\\\ {c}^{2} & =\\frac{13}{3} \\\\ c & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{13}{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, since $c\\in [1,3],$ we take only $c=\\sqrt{\\frac{13}{3}}.$" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291180 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291181 13194139534479 true] [17592186291180 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291182 13194139534479 true] [17592186291180 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291183 13194139534479 true] [17592186291180 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291184 13194139534479 true] [17592186291180 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291185 13194139534479 true] [17592186291180 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534479 true] [17592186291180 1041 "selection" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291180 1104 #edb/ref 17592186291181 13194139534479 true] [17592186291180 1110 #uuid "a3b334d8-e5d7-5e9f-9b88-30720428ea53" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291181 1034 "\\sqrt{\\frac{13}{3}}" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291181 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534479 true] [17592186291181 1111 #uuid "608dc3e1-67e6-5c92-b661-b5c68d8d52a6" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291182 1034 "\\sqrt{13}" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291182 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534479 true] [17592186291182 1111 #uuid "7add7088-8d49-571e-8194-c00c4decc128" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291183 1034 "\\frac{4}{3}" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291183 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534479 true] [17592186291183 1111 #uuid "93a51178-7161-52fa-84a9-17fdb2ed959b" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291184 1034 "\\sqrt{\\frac{5}{3}}" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291184 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534479 true] [17592186291184 1111 #uuid "8e4af557-9916-5223-83b5-ce51677c6bd4" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291185 1034 "\\frac{9}{4}" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291185 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534479 true] [17592186291185 1111 #uuid "0f666665-750c-5c5b-9784-8b04e6b9ec52" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291186 1017 #edb/ref 17592186291187 13194139534479 true] [17592186291186 1089 "q-2490" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291186 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534479 true] [17592186291186 1100 "Find the value of $c$ that satisfies the mean value theorem for integrals for $f(x)=2x$ on the interval $[-1,4].$" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291186 1113 #uuid "7b1cbce3-95c1-5237-b1ab-a61bff4e30ec" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291186 1145 "Applying the mean value theorem for the integrals, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(c)(b-a) & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ f(c) & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4-(-1)}{\\int }_{-1}^{4}2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot ({x}^{2})|}_{-1}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}[{4}^{2}-(-1)^{2}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}(16-1) \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the expression for $f(x)$ to solve for the value of $c:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(c) & =3 \\\\ 2c & =3 \\\\ c & =\\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291187 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291188 13194139534479 true] [17592186291187 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291189 13194139534479 true] [17592186291187 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291190 13194139534479 true] [17592186291187 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291191 13194139534479 true] [17592186291187 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291192 13194139534479 true] [17592186291187 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534479 true] [17592186291187 1041 "selection" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291187 1104 #edb/ref 17592186291191 13194139534479 true] [17592186291187 1110 #uuid "39f35283-6a27-5d2c-bdda-40c78280b7b3" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291188 1034 "-\\frac{1}{2}" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291188 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534479 true] [17592186291188 1111 #uuid "1504336f-ca72-55e7-89a2-b275c283ad75" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291189 1034 "\\frac{2}{3}" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291189 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534479 true] [17592186291189 1111 #uuid "e0135094-0c97-5cc9-a2d3-56be05a12533" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291190 1034 "2" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291190 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534479 true] [17592186291190 1111 #uuid "76bf4f59-7ce5-5812-a44e-e3974eceff31" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291191 1034 "\\frac{3}{2}" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291191 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534479 true] [17592186291191 1111 #uuid "c63a6d83-92cf-585e-ae9c-f7594d5c52db" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291192 1034 "-\\frac{1}{4}" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291192 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534479 true] [17592186291192 1111 #uuid "becccbb7-7a9d-5a74-a329-bf2d3fc9abec" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291193 1017 #edb/ref 17592186291194 13194139534479 true] [17592186291193 1089 "q-30776" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291193 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534479 true] [17592186291193 1100 "Find the average value of the function $g(x)=2{x}^{3}-x-1$ on the interval $[-2,0].$" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291193 1113 #uuid "41a9e5db-75da-5502-afac-88828e98449b" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291193 1145 "Applying the average value formula, we find that the average value of the function is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}g(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{0-(-2)}{\\int }_{-2}^{0}(2{x}^{3}-x-1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{-2}^{0}(2{x}^{3}-x-1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{4}-\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}-x)|}_{-2}^{0} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[(\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot {0}^{4}-\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot {0}^{2}-0)-(\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (-2)^{4}-\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (-2)^{2}-(-2))] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(0-(8-2+2)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(-8) \\\\  & =-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291194 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291195 13194139534479 true] [17592186291194 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291196 13194139534479 true] [17592186291194 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291197 13194139534479 true] [17592186291194 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291198 13194139534479 true] [17592186291194 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291199 13194139534479 true] [17592186291194 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534479 true] [17592186291194 1041 "selection" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291194 1104 #edb/ref 17592186291197 13194139534479 true] [17592186291194 1110 #uuid "d2ae9fb8-6a3d-58fa-892f-b68188b64c4d" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291195 1034 "-8" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291195 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534479 true] [17592186291195 1111 #uuid "672e9ba0-e2be-5a8f-a78a-6bb819f35c51" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291196 1034 "8" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291196 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534479 true] [17592186291196 1111 #uuid "f49fc375-5782-572e-8f2c-7a9cf21ca337" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291197 1034 "-4" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291197 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534479 true] [17592186291197 1111 #uuid "9695b549-f9eb-58e7-b607-8000ed32121d" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291198 1034 "4" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291198 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534479 true] [17592186291198 1111 #uuid "b99675fb-9a01-5b54-8ba3-4589872f6cd6" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291199 1034 "0" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291199 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534479 true] [17592186291199 1111 #uuid "6871dfb7-e709-540e-bc17-835ef63ad935" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291200 1017 #edb/ref 17592186291201 13194139534479 true] [17592186291200 1089 "q-316303" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291200 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534479 true] [17592186291200 1100 "Find the value of $c$ such that the average value of $h(x)=10x-4$ on the interval $[0,c]$ is equal to $6.$ Do not round the answer.\n\n$c=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291200 1113 #uuid "3205321e-1b1e-5760-bd45-12cdf38c44dc" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291200 1145 "To solve for $c,$ we apply the average value formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{h}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}\\,{\\int }_{a}^{b}h(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 6 & =\\frac{1}{c-0}\\,{\\int }_{0}^{c}(10x-4)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 6 & =\\frac{1}{c}(5{x}^{2}-4x){|}_{0}^{c} \\\\ 6 & =\\frac{1}{c}[(5{c}^{2}-4c)-0] \\\\ 6 & =5c-4 \\\\ 10 & =5c \\\\ c & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291201 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291202 13194139534479 true] [17592186291201 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534479 true] [17592186291201 1041 "field-1" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291201 1104 #edb/ref 17592186291202 13194139534479 true] [17592186291201 1110 #uuid "84c8846e-5c7f-57b1-83d0-204ab8f60e18" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291202 1034 "2" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291202 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534479 true] [17592186291202 1111 #uuid "be20bddf-29ff-5395-9415-83419f73355f" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291203 1017 #edb/ref 17592186291204 13194139534479 true] [17592186291203 1089 "q-316307" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291203 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534479 true] [17592186291203 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/assets/64682c2166e3f9fd2366f925330d04f95b54f370fd3d887d1d8aef8885ac35ec.png)\n\nThe graph of the function $f(x),$ which is defined on $[-8,4],$ is shown above. The areas of the regions between the graph and the $x$-axis are $20$, $80$ and $10,$ respectively (from left to right). \n\nFind the average value of $f(x)$ on $[-8,4].$ Do not round the answer.\n\n${f}_{\\text{avg}}=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291203 1113 #uuid "e56f391c-b858-5626-9202-9c04093762c1" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291203 1145 "The average value of a function on a given interval is\n\n$$\n{f}_{\\text{avg}}=\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nHere, we see that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-8}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-20+80-10=50.\n$$\n\nSo, applying the average value formula, we find that the average value is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4-(-8)}\\cdot (50) \\\\  & =\\frac{50}{12} \\\\  & =\\frac{25}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291204 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291205 13194139534479 true] [17592186291204 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534479 true] [17592186291204 1041 "field-1" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291204 1104 #edb/ref 17592186291205 13194139534479 true] [17592186291204 1110 #uuid "60610310-2ac4-5ae9-a341-f1deb1d8f329" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291205 1034 "\\frac{25}{6}" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291205 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534479 true] [17592186291205 1111 #uuid "53eb00fe-4f55-552c-8c93-84099ec474f9" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291206 1017 #edb/ref 17592186291207 13194139534479 true] [17592186291206 1089 "q-3295" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291206 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534479 true] [17592186291206 1100 "Find the average value of the function $f(x)={cos}^{4}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ on the interval $[0,\\pi ].$" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291206 1113 #uuid "11f44eea-f784-5d48-abb5-d216acac4898" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291206 1145 "Applying the average value formula, we find that the average value of the function is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi -0}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{cos}^{4}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe calculate this integral using a substitution $u=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$ Differentiating, we have \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $\\pi $ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $1$ | $-1$ |\n\nWe now substitute and evaluate, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{cos}^{4}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{1}^{-1}{u}^{4}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-{\\frac{1}{\\pi }(\\frac{{u}^{5}}{5})|}_{1}^{-1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{5\\pi }[(-1)^{5}-{1}^{5}] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{5\\pi }(-2) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{5\\pi }.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291207 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291208 13194139534479 true] [17592186291207 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291209 13194139534479 true] [17592186291207 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291210 13194139534479 true] [17592186291207 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291211 13194139534479 true] [17592186291207 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291212 13194139534479 true] [17592186291207 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534479 true] [17592186291207 1041 "selection" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291207 1104 #edb/ref 17592186291209 13194139534479 true] [17592186291207 1110 #uuid "70015f4a-fb2e-51d4-9bbe-ecaecae11cfc" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291208 1034 "\\frac{1}{2\\pi }" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291208 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534479 true] [17592186291208 1111 #uuid "501e7bb8-1edc-5bde-8048-14f0d2014626" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291209 1034 "\\frac{2}{5\\pi }" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291209 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534479 true] [17592186291209 1111 #uuid "614db591-fff5-5c95-8b5b-00b5585aeb6f" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291210 1034 "\\frac{\\pi }{2}" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291210 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534479 true] [17592186291210 1111 #uuid "acebbec0-de5e-5291-9037-2440f4b2be74" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291211 1034 "\\frac{5\\pi }{3}" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291211 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534479 true] [17592186291211 1111 #uuid "a5071f80-8988-568e-bd4f-179679dad0b3" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291212 1034 "0" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291212 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534479 true] [17592186291212 1111 #uuid "08f40b68-4037-5394-9f84-b3da7ec0c446" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291213 1017 #edb/ref 17592186291214 13194139534479 true] [17592186291213 1089 "q-3297" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291213 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534479 true] [17592186291213 1100 "Within  the interval $[0,\\pi ]$, determine the average value of $f(x)=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x.$" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291213 1113 #uuid "3f0b52a6-6395-5fd8-b582-320e2bab87d5" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291213 1145 "Applying the average value formula, we find that the average value of the function is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi -0}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{1}{\\pi }(-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)|}_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }[(-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi )+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\cdot \\pi ))-(-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\cdot 0))] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }[(-2\\cdot (-1)+\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 1)-(-2\\cdot 1+\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 1)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }[(\\frac{5}{2})-(-\\frac{3}{2})] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }(4) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{\\pi }.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291214 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291215 13194139534479 true] [17592186291214 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291216 13194139534479 true] [17592186291214 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291217 13194139534479 true] [17592186291214 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291218 13194139534479 true] [17592186291214 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291219 13194139534479 true] [17592186291214 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534479 true] [17592186291214 1041 "selection" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291214 1104 #edb/ref 17592186291216 13194139534479 true] [17592186291214 1110 #uuid "b1edc742-80f1-586e-bb2b-99ecf431564f" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291215 1034 "\\frac{6}{\\pi }" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291215 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534479 true] [17592186291215 1111 #uuid "6f13272c-a28d-5582-8f59-c64280b3538f" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291216 1034 "\\frac{4}{\\pi }" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291216 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534479 true] [17592186291216 1111 #uuid "771a42fe-844d-5583-aae9-809e4039fca6" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291217 1034 "\\frac{\\pi }{2}" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291217 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534479 true] [17592186291217 1111 #uuid "2a7a1d50-db14-59be-bce0-39111903fe59" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291218 1034 "0" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291218 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534479 true] [17592186291218 1111 #uuid "c5548892-f012-5809-9df2-86631aca3325" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291219 1034 "\\frac{3\\pi }{5}" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291219 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534479 true] [17592186291219 1111 #uuid "7896ec0e-09d6-59e1-888e-42c8793b8da6" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291220 1017 #edb/ref 17592186291221 13194139534479 true] [17592186291220 1089 "q-344521" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291220 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534479 true] [17592186291220 1100 "Find the **exact** value of $c$ that satisfies the mean value theorem for integrals for $f(x)=2{x}^{2}+3$ on the interval $[1,4].$\n\n$c=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291220 1113 #uuid "54fddd2c-8f80-5adf-91bc-e2f8751160b7" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291220 1145 "Applying the mean value theorem for the integrals, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(b-a)f(c) & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ f(c) & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ f(c) & =\\frac{1}{4-1}{\\int }_{1}^{4}(2{x}^{2}+3)\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot (\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{3}+3x)|}_{1}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[(\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot {4}^{3}+3\\cdot 4)-(\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot {1}^{3}+3\\cdot 1)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}(\\frac{164}{3}-\\frac{11}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}(51) \\\\  & =17.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the expression for $f(x)$ to solve for the value of $c:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(c) & =17 \\\\ 2{c}^{2}+3 & =17 \\\\ 2{c}^{2} & =14 \\\\ {c}^{2} & =7 \\\\ c & =\\pm \\sqrt{7}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, since $c\\in [1,4],$ we take only $c=\\sqrt{7}.$" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291221 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291222 13194139534479 true] [17592186291221 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291223 13194139534479 true] [17592186291221 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534479 true] [17592186291221 1041 "field-1" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291221 1104 #edb/ref 17592186291222 13194139534479 true] [17592186291221 1110 #uuid "dd9a421f-36bc-5517-8190-6238a918c86a" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291222 1034 "\\sqrt{7}" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291222 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534479 true] [17592186291222 1111 #uuid "42cf896a-ed28-59ad-996c-fdc4c59a08f9" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291223 1034 "2" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291223 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534479 true] [17592186291223 1111 #uuid "1df61f05-3477-592f-aa29-d9dddd2776b1" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291224 1017 #edb/ref 17592186291225 13194139534479 true] [17592186291224 1089 "q-344574" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291224 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534479 true] [17592186291224 1100 "Find the value of $c$ such that the average value of $h(x)=4x-6$ on the interval $[0,c]$ is equal to $2.$ Do not round the answer.\n\n$c=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291224 1113 #uuid "81417885-cdad-533c-9fc9-c94ac29cbb8f" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291224 1145 "To solve for $c,$ we apply the average value formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{h}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}\\,{\\int }_{a}^{b}h(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 2 & =\\frac{1}{c-0}\\,{\\int }_{0}^{c}(4x-6)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 2 & =\\frac{1}{c}(2{x}^{2}-6x){|}_{0}^{c} \\\\ 2 & =\\frac{1}{c}[(2{c}^{2}-6c)-0] \\\\ 2 & =2c-6 \\\\ 8 & =2c \\\\ c & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291225 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291226 13194139534479 true] [17592186291225 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534479 true] [17592186291225 1041 "field-1" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291225 1104 #edb/ref 17592186291226 13194139534479 true] [17592186291225 1110 #uuid "665f6f74-7c53-5525-b834-a4ef14924401" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291226 1034 "4" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291226 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534479 true] [17592186291226 1111 #uuid "bb682257-5174-5d80-b4de-46a119f65902" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291227 1017 #edb/ref 17592186291228 13194139534479 true] [17592186291227 1089 "q-344596" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291227 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534479 true] [17592186291227 1100 "The **exact** value of $c$ such that the average value of $f(x)=6{x}^{2}-8x-10$ on the interval $[0,c]$ is equal to $-12$ is\n\n$c=$\n{{field-1}}." 13194139534479 true] [17592186291227 1113 #uuid "bfc3ffe0-eb79-55a0-9876-0723bc5ad393" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291227 1145 "To solve for $c,$ we apply the average value formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -12 & =\\frac{1}{c-0}{\\int }_{0}^{c}(6{x}^{2}-8x-10)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -12 & ={\\frac{1}{c}(2{x}^{3}-4{x}^{2}-10x)|}_{0}^{c} \\\\ -12 & =\\frac{1}{c}[(2{c}^{3}-4{c}^{2}-10c)-0] \\\\ -12 & =2{c}^{2}-4c-10 \\\\ 0 & =2{c}^{2}-4c+2 \\\\ 0 & ={c}^{2}-2c+1 \\\\ 0 & =(c-1)^{2} \\\\ c & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the value of $c$ is \n\n$$\nc=1.\n$$" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291228 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291229 13194139534479 true] [17592186291228 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291230 13194139534479 true] [17592186291228 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534479 true] [17592186291228 1041 "field-1" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291228 1104 #edb/ref 17592186291230 13194139534479 true] [17592186291228 1110 #uuid "f0b1da21-91a7-5b46-85c0-256a1c75b6d1" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291229 1034 "2" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291229 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534479 true] [17592186291229 1111 #uuid "c039ea78-e776-5206-8e89-f17e9e3aa758" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291230 1034 "1" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291230 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534479 true] [17592186291230 1111 #uuid "9debab67-805d-5409-b59d-638c831040c2" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291231 1017 #edb/ref 17592186291232 13194139534479 true] [17592186291231 1089 "q-344598" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291231 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534479 true] [17592186291231 1100 "The **exact** value of $c$ such that the average value of $f(x)=12{x}^{2}-24x+1$ on the interval $[0,c]$ is equal to $-8$ is\n\n$c=$\n{{field-1}}." 13194139534479 true] [17592186291231 1113 #uuid "68a98d05-b09e-5226-82dd-37169f58ec4d" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291231 1145 "To solve for $c,$ we apply the average value formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -8 & =\\frac{1}{c-0}{\\int }_{0}^{c}(12{x}^{2}-24x+1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -8 & ={\\frac{1}{c}(4{x}^{3}-12{x}^{2}+x)|}_{0}^{c} \\\\ -8 & =\\frac{1}{c}[(4{c}^{3}-12{c}^{2}+c)-0] \\\\ -8 & =4{c}^{2}-12c+1 \\\\ 0 & =4{c}^{2}-12c+9 \\\\ 0 & =(2c-3)^{2} \\\\ c & =\\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the value of $c$ is \n\n$$\nc=\\frac{3}{2}.\n$$" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291232 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291233 13194139534479 true] [17592186291232 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291234 13194139534479 true] [17592186291232 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534479 true] [17592186291232 1041 "field-1" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291232 1104 #edb/ref 17592186291234 13194139534479 true] [17592186291232 1110 #uuid "ffc0bc94-8123-546e-8175-7938bf455d85" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291233 1034 "2" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291233 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534479 true] [17592186291233 1111 #uuid "37ee6230-84ad-54de-b402-7dd832678a23" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291234 1034 "\\frac{3}{2}" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291234 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534479 true] [17592186291234 1111 #uuid "78547917-0767-523a-a258-e79f3981f9a7" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291235 1017 #edb/ref 17592186291236 13194139534479 true] [17592186291235 1089 "q-344601" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291235 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534479 true] [17592186291235 1100 "The **exact** value of $c$ such that the average value of $f(x)=-15\\sqrt{x}+6$ on the interval $[0,c]$ is equal to $-4$ is\n\n$c=$\n{{field-1}}." 13194139534479 true] [17592186291235 1113 #uuid "b6a588a9-c8e7-5455-809a-9dba63f139de" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291235 1145 "To solve for $c,$ we apply the average value formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -4 & =\\frac{1}{c-0}{\\int }_{0}^{c}(-15\\sqrt{x}+6)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -4 & ={\\frac{1}{c}(-10{x}^{3/2}+6x)|}_{0}^{c} \\\\ -4 & =\\frac{1}{c}[(-10{c}^{3/2}+6c)-0] \\\\ -4 & =-10\\sqrt{c}+6 \\\\ -10 & =-10\\sqrt{c} \\\\ 1 & =\\sqrt{c} \\\\ c & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the value of $c$ is \n\n$$\nc=1.\n$$" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291236 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291237 13194139534479 true] [17592186291236 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534479 true] [17592186291236 1041 "field-1" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291236 1104 #edb/ref 17592186291237 13194139534479 true] [17592186291236 1110 #uuid "f670734c-e70c-5e50-9f50-eb41ca3c8b5f" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291237 1034 "1" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291237 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534479 true] [17592186291237 1111 #uuid "0c04a6a2-8383-58d8-b809-c27bf88a46af" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291238 1017 #edb/ref 17592186291239 13194139534479 true] [17592186291238 1089 "q-344648" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291238 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534479 true] [17592186291238 1100 "Find the average value ${f}_{\\text{avg}}$ of the function $f(x)={cos}^{6}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ on the interval $[0,\\pi ].$ Do not round the answer.\n\n${f}_{\\text{avg}}=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291238 1113 #uuid "752704cb-a8ad-55ac-ac26-51b58834ab35" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291238 1145 "Applying the average value formula, we find that the average value of the function is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi -0}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{cos}^{6}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe calculate this integral using a substitution $u=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$ Differentiating, we have \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $\\pi $ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $1$ | $-1$ |\n\nWe now substitute and evaluate, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{cos}^{6}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{1}^{-1}{u}^{6}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-{\\frac{1}{\\pi }(\\frac{{u}^{7}}{7})|}_{1}^{-1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{7\\pi }[(-1)^{7}-{1}^{7}] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{7\\pi }(-2) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{7\\pi }.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291239 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291240 13194139534479 true] [17592186291239 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534479 true] [17592186291239 1041 "field-1" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291239 1104 #edb/ref 17592186291240 13194139534479 true] [17592186291239 1110 #uuid "43776673-5b88-5afd-9826-30b5c8f2c3f3" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291240 1034 "\\frac{2}{7\\pi}" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291240 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534479 true] [17592186291240 1111 #uuid "27b54b43-3c84-5656-be36-ea9c956fb491" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291241 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291242 13194139534479 true] [17592186291241 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291243 13194139534479 true] [17592186291241 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534479 true] [17592186291241 1041 "field-1" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291241 1104 #edb/ref 17592186291243 13194139534479 true] [17592186291241 1110 #uuid "5cb2a37e-a07b-582d-a149-401211fb4920" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291242 1034 "1" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291242 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534479 true] [17592186291242 1111 #uuid "fec2d609-89f1-5db6-a5a4-f9f16735720c" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291243 1034 "0" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291243 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534479 true] [17592186291243 1111 #uuid "90e1e010-6034-58c1-8d4a-fe3c6b05416a" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291244 1017 #edb/ref 17592186291245 13194139534479 true] [17592186291244 1089 "q-344699" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291244 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534479 true] [17592186291244 1100 "A biologist found that the population $P$ of some algae in a container can be modeled by the function $P(t)=150+10\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi t}{3}),$ where $t$ is the number of hours after $9$ a.m. Find the average number of algae during the period from $9$ a.m. to $3$ p.m. Do not round the answer.\n\n${P}_{\\text{avg}}=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291244 1113 #uuid "ee5b6f8d-9d14-51d5-8a0b-93a2327f9b03" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291244 1145 "Since the function is valid starting from $9$ A.M., we can conclude our interval is $[0,6].$\n\nApplying the average value formula, we find that the average value of the function is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}P(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6-0}{\\int }_{0}^{6}(150+10\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi t}{3}))\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\frac{1}{6}(150t-\\frac{30}{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi \\,t}{3}))|}_{0}^{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}[(150\\cdot 6-\\frac{30}{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi \\cdot 6}{3}))-(150\\cdot 0-\\frac{30}{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi \\cdot 0}{3}))] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}[(900-\\frac{30}{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\pi ))-(-\\frac{30}{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0))] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}[(900-\\frac{30}{\\pi }\\cdot 1)+\\frac{30}{\\pi }\\cdot 1] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}(900) \\\\  & =150.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291245 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291246 13194139534479 true] [17592186291245 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291247 13194139534479 true] [17592186291245 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534479 true] [17592186291245 1041 "field-1" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291245 1104 #edb/ref 17592186291246 13194139534479 true] [17592186291245 1110 #uuid "76b46926-458b-5be2-9489-1f12d1692d13" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291246 1034 "150" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291246 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534479 true] [17592186291246 1111 #uuid "d34dcc96-12a5-59ad-aa71-0e852674d4a5" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291247 1034 "160" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291247 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534479 true] [17592186291247 1111 #uuid "9fd8abde-cdb2-5b01-8878-ff82a8f75d7f" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291248 1017 #edb/ref 17592186291249 13194139534479 true] [17592186291248 1089 "q-344708" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291248 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534479 true] [17592186291248 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/assets/c2e43e711a8c3973e080da7ee0e547b3fdec20ba4536ff7f79f21e8e4683c493.png)\n\nThe graph of the function $f(x),$ which is defined on $[-1,10],$ is shown above. It consists of three line segments and the arc of the semi-circle centered at $(7,0)$ with radius $2.$ \n\nFind the average value ${f}_{\\text{avg}}$ of $f(x)$ on $[1,9].$ Do not round the answer.\n\n${f}_{\\text{avg}}=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291248 1113 #uuid "61b15f80-13fd-5c4c-8961-5d56e0ad54f3" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291248 1145 "The average value of a function on a given interval $[a,b]$ is \n\n$$\n{f}_{\\text{avg}}=\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nUsing the additive property of the definite integral, we write\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{1}^{9}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={{{\\int }_{1}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{1}}+{{{\\int }_{5}^{9}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{-{A}_{2}}.\n$$\n\nThe 1st integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [1,5].$ The corresponding region consists of two right triangles, so we find the total area by adding their areas:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 4\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe 2nd integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [5,9].$ The corresponding region is a semi-circle, so we find the area using the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\pi {r}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\pi \\cdot {2}^{2} \\\\  & =2\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the region lies below the $x$-axis, we have \n\n$$\n{\\int }_{5}^{9}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-{A}_{2}=-2\\pi .\n$$\n\nSo, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{9}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={A}_{1}-{A}_{2} \\\\  & =6-2\\pi \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the formula for the average value, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9-1}\\cdot (6-2\\pi ) \\\\  & =\\frac{6-2\\pi }{8} \\\\  & =\\frac{3-\\pi }{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291249 1000 #edb/ref 1759