.$ The corresponding region is a triangle, so we find the area using the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{2}bh \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 4\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the region lies below the $x$-axis, we have \n\n$$\n{\\int }_{1}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-{A}_{1}=-4.\n$$\n\nThe 2nd integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [5,9].$ The corresponding region is a triangle, so we find the area using the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}bh \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 4\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have \n\n$$\n{\\int }_{5}^{9}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={A}_{2}=6.\n$$\n\nSo, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{9}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-{A}_{1}+{A}_{2} \\\\  & =-4+6 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the formula for the average value, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9-1}\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291253 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291254 13194139534479 true] [17592186291253 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534479 true] [17592186291253 1041 "field-1" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291253 1104 #edb/ref 17592186291254 13194139534479 true] [17592186291253 1110 #uuid "f31cc2e1-7c27-5487-becd-f009ec461d37" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291254 1034 "\\frac{1}{4}" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291254 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534479 true] [17592186291254 1111 #uuid "b7713f75-7c35-58f6-be4b-00d123d352a7" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291255 1017 #edb/ref 17592186291256 13194139534479 true] [17592186291255 1089 "q-344716" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291255 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534479 true] [17592186291255 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/assets/101c319f12d73a4efaef385850b81b79402aaa5a1b900f1876837ff7045b0dd5.png)\n\nThe graph of the function $f(x),$ which is defined on $[-3,7],$ is shown above. It consists of line segments.\n\nFind the average value ${f}_{\\text{avg}}$ of $f(x)$ on $[-2,6].$ Do not round the answer.\n\n${f}_{\\text{avg}}=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291255 1113 #uuid "ba48c80d-2444-54cc-88a7-d142c12ecb2a" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291255 1145 "The average value of a function on a given interval $[a,b]$ is \n\n$$\n{f}_{\\text{avg}}=\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nUsing the additive property of the definite integral, we write\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-2}^{6}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={{{\\int }_{-2}^{2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{1}}+{{{\\int }_{2}^{6}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{-{A}_{2}}.\n$$\n\nThe 1st integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [-2,2].$ The corresponding region is a triangle, so we find the area using the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{2}bh \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 4\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have \n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-2}^{2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={A}_{1}=2.\n$$\n\nThe 2nd integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [2,6].$ The corresponding region is a triangle, so we find the area using the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}bh \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 4\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the region lies below the $x$-axis, we have \n\n$$\n{\\int }_{2}^{6}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-{A}_{2}=-4.\n$$\n\nSo, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-2}^{6}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={A}_{1}-{A}_{2} \\\\  & =2-4 \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the formula for the average value, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6-(-2)}\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{8} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534479 true] [17592186291256 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291257 13194139534479 true] [175921862